    "text": "To determine the number of yellow leaves Bronson collects, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of leaves collected.\n2. Determine the number of brown and green leaves.\n3. Subtract the number of brown and green leaves from the total to find the number of yellow leaves.\n\nFirst, let's find the total number of leaves collected:\n\\[ 12 \\text{ (Thursday)} + 13 \\text{ (Friday)} = 25 \\text{ leaves} \\]\n\nNext, we calculate the number of brown leaves, which is 20% of the total leaves:\n\\[ 0.20 \\times 25 = 5 \\text{ brown leaves} \\]\n\nThen, we calculate the number of green leaves, which is also 20% of the total leaves:\n\\[ 0.20 \\times 25 = 5 \\text{ green leaves} \\]\n\nNow, we find the number of yellow leaves by subtracting the number of brown and green leaves from the total number of leaves:\n\\[ 25 - 5 - 5 = 15 \\text{ yellow leaves} \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of yellow leaves Bronson collects is \\(\\boxed{15}\\).",
